# E0400: `array` is a RECORD, and a record may only contain valtypes, so its
# element bound is AnyVal. Before the val/ref split its `of` was declared
# Any.generic and a reftype element was accepted at the declaration -- the
# record-containment rule was stated in the spec and enforced nowhere.
main: function is {
    a: (array of: String to: 2)
    print "len=\{a.length}"
}
